      "id": 1,
      "text": "Maryland Line is the proposed name for a light‑rail line that will run from Silver Spring to New Carrollton, using the old Georgetown Branch rail corridor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple_Line_(Maryland)",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Purple Line name was chosen in 2003 to avoid confusion with Washington Metro’s color‑named lines, after the Ehrlich administration renamed the project the Bi‑County Transitway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple_Line_(Maryland)",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A new general contractor was selected in November 2021, and a new contract was signed in April 2022, marking a fresh start for the Purple Line construction.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple_Line_(Maryland)",
